-- Lexus Velodrome (Mad Track Arena) — Adult Skate Night
-- Hand-entered per Jody's suggestion (2026-08-26). Verified live against the
-- venue's own schedule page (madtrackarena.com/skate-night/) and Lexus
-- Velodrome's public listings the same day: a real, recurring weekly event
-- — Mondays 21+, Thursdays 25+, 8:00-11:00 PM, $10 admission + $5 skate
-- rental (quad skates and rollerblades, limited availability). Venue address:
-- 601 Mack Ave, Detroit, MI 48201 — inside Detroit proper, not a regional
-- addition.
--
-- IMPORTANT — this is a stopgap, not a real recurrence feature: events.
-- is_recurring exists in the schema but nothing on the site actually reads
-- it or expands a weekly rule into calendar days (checked — no front-end
-- logic references it at all). So instead of one row that would only ever
-- show up once, this seeds one row per actual upcoming Monday/Thursday for
-- the next ~12 weeks. That's an honest way to make it show up correctly on
-- the calendar today, but it needs re-running periodically (or a real
-- recurring-event feature built) to keep extending past mid-November 2026 —
-- flagging this rather than pretending it's a permanent fix.
--
-- Also worth knowing: Lexus Velodrome's own site uses individually numbered
-- event pages (lexusvelodrome.com/event/adult-skate-night-30/), which looks
-- like a real WordPress "The Events Calendar" setup — i.e. this could
-- likely become a real automated cron later instead of a hand-seed. Not
-- built tonight; noted here so it isn't forgotten.
--
-- Idempotent: safe to re-run. external_id makes every row a stable upsert
-- target instead of a duplicate on a second run.

insert into events (
  external_id, title, description, category, venue_name_raw,
  start_date, end_date, time_display, is_recurring, is_free, price_from,
  ticket_url, source, note, status
) values

